class.description:
A [ListSettingsServer] is a [SettingsServer] whose settings resource holds a list of entry resources in one typed [Array] property, for example the buses of an audio layout or the personas of a game. The entries are found by their index or by the value of a key property (see [method _get_entry_key]).
Every change of the list or of an entry emits [signal SettingsServer.value_changed] for the list property and, in [constant SettingsServer.APPLY_MODE_IMMEDIATE], applies the settings. The list property is the name that [method SettingsServer.get_dirty_setting_names] and [signal SettingsServer.applied] report.
A list domain can be stored as CSV ([member ProjectSettings.settings/general/default_format], or the format of the domain group [code]settings/<domain>/[/code], set to [constant ResourceTextSerializer.FORMAT_CSV]) if its settings resource has exactly one typed array of resources with simple properties (see [method ResourceTextSerializer.can_serialize] with [constant ResourceTextSerializer.FORMAT_CSV]). The file then has one row per entry. If the domain does not fit, INI is used and a warning is printed once.
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
# voices_settings.gd, listed in settings/startup/custom_servers.
extends ListSettingsServer

func _get_domain() -> StringName:
	return &"voices"

func _get_entry_key() -> StringName:
	return &"voice_name"

func _create_settings() -> Resource:
	return VoiceList.new() # A Resource with "@export var entries: Array[VoiceEntry]".

# Anywhere in the game:
func add_voice():
	var voices = SettingsServerManager.get_server(&"voices")
	var entry = VoiceEntry.new()
	entry.voice_name = "guard"
	voices.add_entry(entry)

	var index = voices.find_entry("guard")
	voices.set_entry_value(index, "pitch", 0.8)
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
// VoicesSettings.cs, listed in settings/startup/custom_servers.
public partial class VoicesSettings : ListSettingsServer
{
    public override StringName _GetDomain() => "voices";

    public override StringName _GetEntryKey() => "voice_name";

    public override Resource _CreateSettings() => new VoiceList();
}

// Anywhere in the game:
var voices = (ListSettingsServer)SettingsServerManager.GetServer("voices");
var entry = new VoiceEntry { VoiceName = "guard" };
voices.AddEntry(entry);

int index = voices.FindEntry("guard");
voices.SetEntryValue(index, "pitch", 0.8f);
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
